WEBVTT

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.280
Karte 10 - Sinking Woman

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.510
<i>20 years ago, a group</i>
<i>of factories was encouraged...</i>

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.620
<i>to build in</i>
<i>the midstream area...</i>

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.590
<i>of the Mangetsu River,</i>
<i>the bay's main tributary.</i>

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.950
<i>It was naturally assumed that</i>
<i>plenty of care would be taken...</i>

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.320
<i>to prevent pollution</i>
<i>from the factories' effluents.</i>

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.230
<i>But the sea was polluted.</i>

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.180
<i>It was a mistake</i>
<i>made by a supposedly...</i>

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.780
<i>strictly managed</i>
<i>wastewater processing plant.</i>

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.340
<i>The mistake went unnoticed</i>
<i>for two years.</i>

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.620
<i>And in that time, a large quantity</i>
<i>of heavy metal toxins...</i>

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.910
<i>was released</i>
<i>into Mikazuki Bay.</i>

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.360
<i>Though he loved her,</i>
<i>Jiro was human.</i>

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.890
<i>He had a family and was</i>
<i>to take over the fishing group.</i>

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.920
<i>And he had a fiancee.</i>

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.430
<i>Her love for him was</i> too <i>much</i>
<i>to bear, and Nagi wept.</i>

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.670
<i>She cried and cried...</i>

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.040
<i>so much that she</i>
<i>nearly blinded herself.</i>

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.550
I'll admit that it took our company
a long time to notice the problem!

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.290
But many of those
made sick...

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.660
by the contaminated fish
from Mikazuki Bay...

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.190
ate them <i>after</i> we had issued
a warning about it!

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.370
Objection!

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.330
The Mikazuki people's livelihood
depends on the fishing industry!

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.600
Eating marine products
from the bay...

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.800
has long been
central to their lives!

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.280
It's nearly 100% certain that
they ate the contaminated fish...

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.610
before the warning was issued!

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.110
Saying they ate them
after it was issued is meaningless!

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.280
It's damn close to perjury!

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.110
Objection sustained.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.020
I will not have you blaming
the injured parties...

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.750
for their condition!

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.420
Y- Yes, Your Honor.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.060
<i>Heavy metal toxemia</i>
<i>produces...</i>

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.490
<i>a range of symptoms</i>
<i>in the human body.</i>

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.340
<i>It's especially marked by sharp pain</i>
<i>in the arm and leg joints,</i>

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.670
<i>to the point</i>
<i>of crippling the patient.</i>

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.380
<i>Abnormalities develop</i>
<i>in the optic nerve,</i>

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.970
<i>which lead to</i>
<i>blurred or double-vision.</i>

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.620
<i>Some develop eczema</i>
<i>and sudden hair loss.</i>

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.550
<i>Others manifest</i>
<i>chronic fever and perspiration.</i>

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.160
<i>The state recognizes "Mikazuki Syndrome"</i>
<i>as a pollution sickness.</i>

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.230
<i>They say it'll take 15 years</i>
<i>for the bay to recover.</i>

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.740
<i>23 dead and 463 severely ill.</i>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.570
<i>With 3,500 claimants, the Mikazuki Bay</i>
<i>pollution trial ended today.</i>

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.440
<i>Victory</i>
<i>It was a complete victory</i>
<i>for the plaintiffs.</i>

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.080
<i>D.L. Chemical was ordered</i>
<i>to pay 50 billion yen in damages...</i>

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.720
<i>towards the cleanup</i>
<i>of Mikazuki Bay.</i>

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.730
<i>A harsh judgement,</i>
<i>as was expected.</i>

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.990
In the bag, as usual!

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.160
Pinoko!

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.600
<i>Money isn't</i>
<i>going to settle this!</i>

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.830
<i>I want to be healthy again!</i>

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.500
<i>Give us back the sea!</i>

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.730
<i>Give us back</i>
<i>our beautiful Mikazuki Bay!</i>

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.300
Give it back!

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.200
Pinoko, where's
the key to the car?

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.670
Dunno.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:49.280
I have an appointment.
The key's not in the usual place.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:51.990
Where are you goin'?

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.020
Downtown.
Someone's waiting for me.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.150
Can I come, too?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.290
No.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.130
Then I don't know
where the key is.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.600
Oh, well. Come, if you wish.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.470
Here it is!

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.890
I'm Sugita from D.L. Chemical.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.090
D.L. Chemical?

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.290
I'm also on the committee
for Mikazuki Syndrome Relief.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.490
Cafe au Lait, please.
With lots of milk!

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.670
As you wish.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.670
Doctor, I ask most urgently
for your help!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.680
This is Dr. Fox,
of Stanley University Hospital,

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.510
whom our company has retained.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:52.580
Dr. Black Jack, I have another favor
to trouble you with.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.980
You're always
such a help to me.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.220
It was back when I was
the chief doctor in a team...

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.950
overseeing land mine disposal
in the Gilnian highlands.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.990
We met by coincidence,
and I convinced the doctor

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.430
to perform some
emergency surgery.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.290
He saved three children
who'd been injured by a mine.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:15.840
He operated on all three at once,
saving valuable time!

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.400
It's dangerous to have
children wait for surgery.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.170
It was risky,
but it was the only choice.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:28.510
And they've grown into fine young
men who are healthy and working.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.380
Will you please help us?

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:35.790
As you know, we've seen
a lot of joint problems...

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.690
in Mikazuki Syndrome victims.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.460
Especially cartilage deformation
and degeneration.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.320
Even with artificial joints,

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.360
it's requiring
very difficult surgery.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.930
Over 300 people require it.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.040
And as the days pass, the likelihood
that more will need it grows.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.440
Of course, the main problem
is a lack of doctors to do this,

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.910
but the truth is that an even more
serious problem has arisen!

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.320
We've performed
30 operations so far,

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.890
and while they appeared
to be successful

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:12.490
none of the patients
have been able to walk again!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.160
There are few cases to study
on heavy metal toxemia.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:19.730
Exactly.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.910
This is the first time we've seen
so many victims at once.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.470
There are too many
unknown factors in this case!

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.180
What do you say, Doctor?

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.450
Would you participate in the
relief committee's medical group...

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.250
as a special consultant?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.580
We've prepared
a retainer for you, in cash.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.150
First, let's get
to the affected area.

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:44.590
I'll decide there
if I want to take this case.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.150
Of... of course.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:55.430
Though Nagi was a mermaid,
she didn't give up on Jiro.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.040
She thought a bit more,

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.710
then dove into the sea
to get him a gift.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.200
Night after night, she dove
into the moonlit waters.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.480
Clinical Chart 10
The Sinking Woman

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:41.310
I don't want to hear
your sad good-byes.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:45.290
So, get on with it
and leave me!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.250
'Cause this hasn't been
the type of love...

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:53.490
where I thought I'd get
back everything.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.240
Gave up all I had
to be with you.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.240
The least you could do
is face me!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.870
As you starve yourself,
you waste away...

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.240
like you're crucified
and dying!

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:26.320
Enrobed in the dark
of my heart...

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:35.170
I take the memories we had, and
throw them out forever!

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.370
Way down deep
inside your sober, searching eyes...

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.110
emerges
a pitch-black shadow that...

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:45.480
reminds me of a god of death.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:49.850
After all,
you never let me see inside...

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.850
see inside that heart of yours.
Oh...

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.220
I must look
like I'm a tiny little child...

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.850
who buries
my head into your lap...

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.300
to cry into your waiting arms.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.960
Just before
I fell apart when I saw...

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:09.870
the sun
peek out of the clouds.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.100
<i>Shin-Mikazuki Station!</i>
<i>Shin-Mikazuki Station!</i>

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.510
Pinoko, wake up. Pinoko.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:46.840
Ooh... Can't eat any more...

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.810
<i>Now arriving on Platform 4...</i>

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:55.680
<i>Next train bound for Fukugami at</i>
<i>18:08 is now a super limited express.</i>

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.520
<i>The Angel Super Express</i>
<i>will arrive at 18:</i>

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.780
Mangetsu Inn
at the Mikazuki Hot Springs.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.690
Sure thing! The Mangetsu Inn!

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:03.660
<i>Taxi</i>
<i>Stand</i>

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.300
Your little girl
can really sleep, huh?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.860
You come to the
Mikazuki Hot Springs often?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.490
No. First time.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.000
Oh. You asked
for the Mangetsu Inn, so...

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.140
Nobody goes there unless
they know this place really well.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.650
The baths are outstanding,
and, uh...

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.620
I chose it at random
from the phone book.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.820
The baths are great. Really!

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.660
This is the road to
the Mikazuki Hot Spring Center.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.500
The Mangetsu Inn's
a little off this.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.400
We're going
onto the mountain road!

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.800
Doctor...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.110
Just sleep.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.340
I gotta pee!

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.480
There's a toilet up the stairs,
on the temple grounds.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:09.620
This temple looks really old!

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:13.330
<i>Hachiman Shrine</i>
It's a Shinto shrine.
Mikazuki Hachiman.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.930
The locals call it
the Mermaid Shrine.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.600
Mermaids?

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:23.330
I hear that the mermaid legend
of Mikazuki beach was pretty famous.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.260
Nowadays,
the shrine's been neglected,

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:27.970
and we're just famous
for the Syndrome.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.180
Oh, little girl!
The toilet's that way!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.480
R... right!

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.030
Well? Pretty amazing, huh?

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:54.800
I think this town would've
been a lot happier...

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.170
if those factories
had never been built here,

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.770
and we just hosted sightseers
coming for the mermaid legend.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.680
May the Doctor's job
turn out all right.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:10.280
May the Doctor
not get a bad illness.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.780
May the Doctor
always treat me nice.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.090
May the Doctor
never cheat on me!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.460
Let's go, Pinoko!

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.550
May he one day
tell me he loves me!

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.930
Coming!
Coming, coming, coming!

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.630
Hello, and welcome
to the Mangetsu Inn.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:43.450
The springs are open-air
and open 24 hours a day.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:46.620
Would you like your dinner first
or after the bath?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.020
Hot spring first!

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:52.220
Very well! Enjoy, and they'll
put a "spring" in your step!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.320
Just kidding!

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:58.830
Don't "spring"
that pun on me!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:00.890
Hey, not bad!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.200
Funny man!

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:08.270
Hey, I hold down this place
by myself, so no making fun of me!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.440
Huh? Alone?

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:12.500
No clerks or waitresses
or geisha or anything?

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:16.080
Right! Which is why
we get hardly any customers!

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:25.620
(singing nonsense)

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:28.630
You picked
a weird inn, Doctor.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.400
But the baths are great,
don't you think?

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:34.940
Yup! Perfect! I ain't
"springing" no complaints!

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:38.100
I'll be very busy,
starting tomorrow.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.540
Just relax here.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.600
Huh? I'm gonna
be here all alone?

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.840
I'll try to get back
as early as I can.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.310
Okay, then!

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:49.680
(singing nonsense)

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:56.020
(singing nonsense)

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.690
Whoa! In there! Get in there!

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:02.300
Busy, busy, busy...

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.560
Hey! Mr. Aruji!

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.370
That tank of water out there
is outstanding!

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.600
Oh, "tank you!"
Just kidding!

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:16.800
Fireflies!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:27.990
Fireflies?

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.790
Y- Yeah, they are.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:30.480
They're pretty...

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:32.690
Yeah! Aren't they?

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:34.590
Here you go.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:39.530
Tsukiko! What's up?
Backlogged with fish again?

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.540
Yeah, I am.

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.300
Will you buy some, Uncle?

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:45.400
Well, let's see
what you've got.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.410
Let's see...
Sea bass... Opaleye...

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.350
Oh, and sea bream, too!
All top-quality stuff!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:55.540
Thanks for bringing them
all the way up here from the beach!

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:58.650
How about 1000 yen
for the lot?

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:01.680
Okay, fine.
Thanks for your business!

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.350
Hang on
and I'll get your money.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:05.550
Sure.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:10.420
(humming nonsense)

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:16.830
You can't eat fish
from Mikazuki Bay.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:21.040
Relax. I'm gonna bury
these things in the ground.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.650
The only talent that girl has
is for catching fish.

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:28.670
She's gotta make
a living somehow.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.680
We all know that, so the folks
down on the beach and I...

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.750
buy her fish,
even if we don't eat them.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.060
But seeing her come in this far,
once every three days...

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:45.460
means less and less people
on the shore are buying from her.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:48.030
One, two, three...

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:56.000
It's terrible. Her legs
get worse and worse...

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.450
and she has to climb
a mountain road!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.680
Her legs are getting worse?

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:04.280
Use it to buy some bread,
Tsukiko.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:06.750
Sure!

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.350
And watch out
for eating raw stuff.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:09.920
Right!

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.820
Watch out in Suisho Valley!

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.560
The road's narrow
from the rock slides lately!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.530
Right!

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:34.950
Tsukiko!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.020
Don't move! Stay still.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.560
Where'd you hit?
Tell me where it hurts.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:50.050
It's okay!
My boss is a doctor!

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.170
How's your elbow?
It's bleeding a bit.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.380
Looks okay.
No vertebrae damaged.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.070
How long has
your knee been like this?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.240
My knee?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.650
How long has it been hurt?

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:12.280
Doctor, do you like
blue pearls?

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:13.620
Hm?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.310
I said you can stay here!

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.760
I have plenty of empty rooms!

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.730
Right!

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.700
Her knee...
It's clearly Mikazuki Syndrome.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:36.530
You know
what blue pearls are, Doc?

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.670
Hm? No.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:42.310
It's an old custom that
when a woman gives a man...

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.750
a blue pearl from Mikazuki Bay,
he has to marry her.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.760
It's a token of her love.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:50.150
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Say what?

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:54.720
Relax! You can't find 'em
anymore, so you're safe!

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.870
Prefectural Hospital 3, huh?

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.000
Oh, I get it!

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.130
You're a doctor, aren't you?

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:09.000
Wow. I've been wondering
what you were since yesterday.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.510
Did the Mikazuki Relief
Committee rope you into this?

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.280
How did you know?

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.880
Because I don't remember
the last time I drove around...

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:21.650
the greatest doctors
from all over the country!

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:25.960
And I've got a feeling in my bones
that you're a good doctor, Mister!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:32.230
Do your best, please. This town's
turning into a giant sick ward!

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.640
I'd like to see Dr. Fox
of the Primary Surgical Department.

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:42.010
The name's Hazama.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.510
<i>I told them I'd hold off</i>
<i>on accepting this case...</i>

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:48.850
<i>until I arrived at the scene.</i>

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:52.520
<i>But the truth is that I intended</i>
<i>to accept it from the start.</i>

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.320
<i>The sheer variety of poisoning</i>
<i>diseases interested me,</i>

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:01.860
<i>and I have a great hatred of</i>
<i>the massive crime of pollution...</i>

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:06.560
<i>committed by a society which puts</i>
<i>corporate profits before all else.</i>

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.630
Doctor! You've come
at a most opportune time!

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.510
We're about
to start a meeting.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:18.680
Could you please attend?

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:22.210
I still haven't said
that I'd accept this case.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.220
At least see what sort
of work we're doing!

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:27.790
We can talk afterwards.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.230
12-year-old girl in pediatrics
in the East Ward.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:36.160
Postoperative progress
on her patella and cartilage...

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:39.960
has been very good
from a surgical standpoint.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.060
However, the patient has suffered
stomach pains of unknown origin,

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.940
which come in 10-minute
intervals, and I have ordered...

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:47.170
continual dosage with anticholinergic
drugs as an emergency treatment.

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:49.800
However, it's had no effect.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.970
Doctors,
I'd like your opinions.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.910
Have you noticed
any abdominal inflammation?

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.610
Is there a chance
it's a virus?

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.980
There's no inflammation.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:01.280
I couldn't find
any signs of a virus.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:04.320
How about
intravenous steroids?

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:09.460
I heard it helped a 72-year-old man
with similar symptoms in Room Eight.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.760
I suggest
you forget the steroids.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:15.500
The old man
died this morning!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:20.040
Let me introduce you.
This is Dr. Kuro Hazama.

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:21.830
I'm Hazama.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:27.000
As far as I know, there is
no more skillful a surgeon...

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.520
than Mr. Hazama here.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.780
It's not official yet,
but I expect him...

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.720
to be part of our staff
starting tomorrow.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:41.090
Yes. What? I'll be right there!

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:45.590
That little girl's crashing!
She may code at any minute!

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.100
Excuse me!

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.970
Doctor, come with me.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:58.210
Meeting canceled!
We'll reconvene tomorrow afternoon!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.520
Have we met somewhere before?

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:09.580
No.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:15.990
Where was it?

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.540
She's in V-Fib! Countershock!

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:25.970
Ready, Doctor.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:32.370
Reset to 300 joules!
Let's do it again!

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.120
10 milligrams of Bosmin!

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.820
Add 250 milliliters
of sodium bicarb!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.190
How about looking
inside her abdomen?

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:52.730
Right now?

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:56.560
Doctor, it's impossible.
It'll strain the heart too much.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.340
An antiarrhythmic
should reduce...

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:01.740
the stress on her
cardiopulmonary functions.

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:06.180
I see. What do you say,
Dr. Hayashi?

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:07.200
Shall we try it?

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:11.910
But, well... I don't think I can
handle the operation in this case.

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:15.790
What do you say, Dr. Hazama?
Will you do it?

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:12.910
It hurts... It hurts...

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.890
<i>We commenced abdominal</i>
<i>surgery on the little girl.</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:30.450
<i>First, we checked from the duodenum</i>
<i>second position to the jejunum.</i>

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:32.830
<i>They're easy spots to overlook</i>
<i>on a CT scan or an MRI.</i>

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:35.300
External appearance
seems normal.

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:37.730
Time?

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:38.970
Eight minutes have elapsed.

00:23:39.010 --> 00:23:39.870
Confirm vitals.

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:40.810
Vitals!

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:45.480
Pulse: 82!
Pressure: 114 over 60!

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.510
I'm going in.
Another scalpel, please.

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:54.760
<i>The patient can only take</i>
<i>20 minutes of this, at most.</i>

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:59.550
<i>If the problem isn't in her terminal</i>
<i>illeum, we'll have to close her up.</i>

00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:05.130
<i>And this abdominal surgery</i>
<i>will have been for nothing.</i>

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:09.860
<i>This operation had to wring</i>
<i>as much data from her as it could.</i>

00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:15.870
<i>My first case of Mikazuki</i>
<i>Syndrome was proving...</i>

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:17.570
<i>extremely difficult</i>
<i>and dangerous.</i>

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:19.550
Doctor, look!

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:20.380
Yes.

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:23.350
It's like a bubble,
or a fish egg.

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:25.380
It hurts!

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:28.820
Removing it.

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:36.360
Noriko...

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:37.290
Non-chan...

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:43.460
Mr. O-Hashi.

00:24:44.770 --> 00:24:47.110
Your daughter's surgery
was a success.

00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:50.910
Those stomach aches
should be gone for good.

00:24:51.110 --> 00:24:53.780
This is Dr. Hazama,
who performed the surgery.

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:55.310
He was magnificent.

00:24:57.590 --> 00:24:59.880
Thank you so much, Doctor!

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:01.410
Thank you so much!

00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:04.950
Now I remember!
It's Black Jack!

00:25:31.050 --> 00:25:34.650
I know I'm late! Sorry!

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:36.990
What's this vital problem
you have to talk about?

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:41.530
I was planning to start him
on full rotation tomorrow,

00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:45.330
so I was hoping to let
the doctor go home early.

00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:49.400
I'm sorry. Someone
blabbed to the head office.

00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:53.100
They've called
an emergency board meeting.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:54.570
Blabbed about what?

00:25:55.410 --> 00:25:57.610
About an unlicensed
doctor being on...

00:25:57.650 --> 00:25:59.910
the Mikazuki Syndrome
Relief Committee.

00:26:00.050 --> 00:26:00.840
Hm?

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:05.890
I thought introducing him
to the staff as Hazama...

00:26:05.920 --> 00:26:07.290
would make things okay.

00:26:09.090 --> 00:26:14.150
You said yourself we were to get
the very best surgeons for this!

00:26:14.460 --> 00:26:16.760
Yes, yes, of course I did!

00:26:16.800 --> 00:26:19.200
But an unlicensed doctor
could ruin us!

00:26:19.230 --> 00:26:21.200
Our company would face
criticism at the best of times,

00:26:21.240 --> 00:26:23.930
but we can't afford
any more scandals!

00:26:23.970 --> 00:26:26.340
I know how much
you were counting on this,

00:26:26.370 --> 00:26:29.280
and I really thought
I could keep it secret, but...

00:26:29.310 --> 00:26:32.110
we <i>need</i> Dr. Black Jack here!

00:26:32.150 --> 00:26:33.810
I know! I know!

00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:37.970
Oh, great. Anyway, the president's
making his decision about this.

00:26:38.020 --> 00:26:40.350
Oh, my head's
gonna roll for this.

00:26:40.390 --> 00:26:41.650
I can arrange that!

00:26:41.690 --> 00:26:42.820
Sure...

00:26:44.630 --> 00:26:46.250
I'll drop this case.

00:26:49.930 --> 00:26:54.800
I foolishly forgot that I must
never venture out into the sunlight.

00:26:55.770 --> 00:26:56.790
Doctor...

00:26:58.010 --> 00:27:01.100
I have my own way
of doing things, don't I?

00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:02.540
Doctor!

00:27:03.950 --> 00:27:05.940
Excuse me, Dr. Fox.

00:27:09.050 --> 00:27:11.450
Doctor!
Dr. Hazama, take this!

00:27:11.490 --> 00:27:13.720
The retainer
we prepared for you!

00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:15.550
Please... Please, take this!

00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:22.430
I'll just take my fee
for today's operation.

00:27:38.650 --> 00:27:39.610
Doctor!

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:43.850
Goin' home?
C'mon, take my cab!

00:27:44.520 --> 00:27:47.550
Hey, no way!
No line jumping!

00:27:47.590 --> 00:27:49.560
Sorry! He's a relative! Sorry!

00:27:49.590 --> 00:27:51.080
You never watch this stuff!
Sheesh!

00:27:51.130 --> 00:27:52.820
Sorry about this!

00:27:56.430 --> 00:27:59.420
So, here you are again!
Mangetsu Inn, right?

00:27:59.570 --> 00:28:00.060
Yes.

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:04.140
So, what time should I pick you up
tomorrow morning?

00:28:07.040 --> 00:28:07.770
Stop!

00:28:07.810 --> 00:28:10.040
Huh? Uh, sure!

00:28:13.750 --> 00:28:14.770
Wait here!

00:28:15.450 --> 00:28:16.140
Sure!

00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:28.720
It... hurts.

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:31.900
It hurts.

00:28:37.070 --> 00:28:39.840
What's wrong?
Are you in pain?

00:28:39.870 --> 00:28:40.640
Can't you walk?

00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:44.800
Doctor... Doctor, it's you...

00:28:45.610 --> 00:28:49.070
Does this leg hurt, too?
You were walking on it yesterday.

00:28:49.450 --> 00:28:52.150
I caught a lot
of great fish today.

00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:53.480
I'm sure
I'll sell them fast!

00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:58.690
Gotta go.
My customers are waiting.

00:29:01.330 --> 00:29:03.060
Sorry about this.

00:29:04.530 --> 00:29:06.760
It's all right. You can't stand.

00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:07.830
Don't push yourself.

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:10.530
You're so warm.

00:29:15.080 --> 00:29:15.970
Let's get going.

00:29:18.950 --> 00:29:20.470
Go where she tells you to.

00:29:20.950 --> 00:29:22.140
We're selling fish.

00:29:22.180 --> 00:29:24.080
Uh, sure! Sure!

00:29:28.590 --> 00:29:29.560
That way!

00:29:29.590 --> 00:29:30.150
Sure thing!

00:29:32.760 --> 00:29:33.350
This way!

00:29:34.260 --> 00:29:35.020
Okay!

00:29:41.970 --> 00:29:45.410
Fish for sale! Fish for sale!

00:29:45.440 --> 00:29:47.170
Fish for sale!

00:29:47.610 --> 00:29:49.080
Hey, Tsukiko!

00:29:49.240 --> 00:29:51.740
That thin girl was here
the day before last.

00:29:51.980 --> 00:29:55.070
She says you should take the money
and they'll put you...

00:29:55.120 --> 00:29:57.410
in a nursing home
in Tama-something in Tokyo.

00:29:58.790 --> 00:30:00.350
Want some fish, ma'am?

00:30:00.890 --> 00:30:03.290
Sorry, my family
don't eat fish no more.

00:30:06.830 --> 00:30:09.490
Fish! Fish for sale!

00:30:10.230 --> 00:30:11.490
Now where?

00:30:11.530 --> 00:30:12.000
That way!

00:30:13.900 --> 00:30:17.770
Sorry, Tsuki, dear. My son and his wife
told me not to buy fish anymore.

00:30:18.110 --> 00:30:20.940
It's not much,
but take my secret savings...

00:30:21.380 --> 00:30:22.570
I don't want it!

00:30:28.420 --> 00:30:30.880
Fish for sale!

00:30:30.920 --> 00:30:33.680
Opaleye! Sea bream!
All kinds for sale!

00:30:34.160 --> 00:30:37.180
Fish! Fish for sale!

00:30:37.230 --> 00:30:40.220
Fish! Fish for sale!

00:30:40.930 --> 00:30:44.300
Genuine fresh
Mikazuki Bay fish!

00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:48.090
Opaleye! Sea bream!
All kinds for sale!

00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:52.540
I'll go home now.

00:30:54.940 --> 00:30:57.310
Doc! Where are you going?

00:30:57.550 --> 00:30:58.530
This way!

00:31:00.850 --> 00:31:01.710
That way.

00:31:07.320 --> 00:31:08.910
This is my home.

00:31:17.930 --> 00:31:19.870
Welcome to my humble home.

00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:22.990
Shall I make us some tea?

00:31:24.210 --> 00:31:25.140
By all means.

00:31:28.510 --> 00:31:29.410
Your tea.

00:31:29.910 --> 00:31:30.500
Thank you.

00:31:35.150 --> 00:31:36.280
Is something funny?

00:31:37.550 --> 00:31:41.010
I figured you were
a gentle man, like Nagi did.

00:31:44.460 --> 00:31:48.660
Jiro was quiet, too,
but Nagi could tell.

00:31:48.700 --> 00:31:51.530
That's why she played
her flute for Jiro.

00:31:52.230 --> 00:31:55.430
Di-dodo-di.
Di-do-do-doo...

00:31:55.470 --> 00:31:58.030
It was a lovely tune.

00:31:58.070 --> 00:32:00.870
And she danced
a pretty dance for him, too!

00:32:01.540 --> 00:32:02.640
The mermaid dance!

00:32:03.750 --> 00:32:06.110
Da-di-di-dee-da-di...

00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:08.810
Da-di-di-dee-da-di...

00:32:08.850 --> 00:32:11.110
Di-la-la-la-la-laa...

00:32:19.630 --> 00:32:20.920
It hurts!

00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:34.400
- Take that!
- I gotcha!

00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:36.410
- Gotcha now!
- Gotcha now!

00:32:41.320 --> 00:32:42.250
Now for the kill!

00:32:42.280 --> 00:32:43.380
Pinoko!

00:32:44.750 --> 00:32:46.720
Yes, Doctor! Coming!

00:32:47.020 --> 00:32:47.990
Prep for surgery!

00:32:48.460 --> 00:32:51.050
Prepare a 500cc
Isojin solution!

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:54.620
Right when I was about
to win the stupid game...

00:32:55.300 --> 00:32:58.060
Manager, I'm sorry,
but I'd like another room.

00:32:58.570 --> 00:32:59.860
Upstairs, then down!

00:33:00.670 --> 00:33:01.660
The hall, I mean.

00:33:01.700 --> 00:33:03.300
This is no time for jokes!

00:33:08.780 --> 00:33:12.440
Primary Surgical Unit,
Dr. Fox, please pick up line 6.

00:33:13.080 --> 00:33:16.780
Primary Surgical Unit,
Dr. Fox, please pick up line 6.

00:33:19.820 --> 00:33:21.410
Ah, Dr. Black Jack!

00:33:21.990 --> 00:33:25.820
Could you spare me
a couple of artificial joints?

00:33:25.860 --> 00:33:28.830
I see... Does the patient
have Mikazuki Syndrome?

00:33:29.460 --> 00:33:32.130
Yes. Female, approximately
19 years old.

00:33:32.170 --> 00:33:34.530
Blood-type AB,
Rh factor positive.

00:33:35.270 --> 00:33:37.430
Suffering palpitations
with patellar abnormalities.

00:33:37.470 --> 00:33:40.200
Still relatively light
on the right knee,

00:33:40.240 --> 00:33:41.730
but severe on the left.

00:33:42.340 --> 00:33:46.640
Bring her here!
I'll have everything ready!

00:33:46.680 --> 00:33:48.240
No, I can't.

00:33:48.820 --> 00:33:51.750
I'll take responsibility!
Please bring her!

00:33:56.560 --> 00:33:59.360
I understand.
I'll send them over at once.

00:33:59.390 --> 00:34:00.620
Tell me where you are.

00:34:01.760 --> 00:34:04.630
I appreciate it.
I'm in your debt.

00:34:05.570 --> 00:34:08.870
The hell you are!
I'm in <i>your</i> debt!

00:34:13.710 --> 00:34:15.730
Heave-ho!

00:34:15.780 --> 00:34:16.870
Here... we... go!

00:34:16.910 --> 00:34:18.540
Got it! Got it!

00:34:25.490 --> 00:34:26.180
Carry me!

00:34:34.060 --> 00:34:35.960
We'll be starting
your surgery soon.

00:34:36.630 --> 00:34:37.690
Surgery?

00:34:38.500 --> 00:34:40.690
Yes, on your legs.

00:34:40.870 --> 00:34:43.390
If it works,
you'll be able to walk again.

00:34:43.710 --> 00:34:44.760
Walk...

00:34:44.940 --> 00:34:48.140
Yes, walk. And swim.

00:34:49.110 --> 00:34:50.840
I can go back to the sea.

00:34:51.210 --> 00:34:52.040
You can.

00:34:52.580 --> 00:34:57.140
(makes sound of waves)

00:34:57.720 --> 00:35:01.590
Doctor, someday,
I'll be your bride!

00:35:03.420 --> 00:35:04.820
I'll bring you a blue pearl.

00:35:11.300 --> 00:35:14.630
<i>I began the operation</i>
<i>with the more damaged left patella.</i>

00:35:15.740 --> 00:35:17.860
<i>While we were</i>
<i>in a room in a small inn,</i>

00:35:17.910 --> 00:35:19.900
<i>we'd set up</i>
<i>a fair amount of equipment.</i>

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:24.030
<i>Dr. Fox had brought</i>
<i>not only the artificial joints,</i>

00:35:24.080 --> 00:35:26.600
<i>but all the equipment I'd need</i>
<i>from the hospital.</i>

00:35:28.180 --> 00:35:29.210
It wasn't me.

00:35:30.490 --> 00:35:33.350
Mr. Sugita said
we should do it.

00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:35.610
Relax, it'll be fine.

00:35:35.660 --> 00:35:38.090
Nothing'll happen, as long as
the home office doesn't find out.

00:35:45.400 --> 00:35:47.060
As expected,
there's been a deformation...

00:35:47.100 --> 00:35:48.260
of the patellar cartilage.

00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:51.500
Typical presentation
of Mikazuki Syndrome.

00:35:52.440 --> 00:35:53.600
I'll implant
the artificial joint.

00:35:54.510 --> 00:35:56.070
Implanting artificial joint!

00:35:59.750 --> 00:36:02.980
Um, anything
we can do to help?

00:36:03.020 --> 00:36:05.420
No! No!
Now stay out of the way!

00:36:11.090 --> 00:36:13.620
<i>Nagi thought to herself...</i>

00:36:13.660 --> 00:36:17.390
<i>Jiro was cold to her</i>
<i>because she had a tail.</i>

00:36:18.030 --> 00:36:21.260
<i>So Nagi prayed to</i>
<i>the Lord of the Dragon Palace.</i>

00:36:22.270 --> 00:36:28.140
<i>"Please, change my tail</i>
<i>into two legs, like humans have."</i>

00:36:28.610 --> 00:36:31.480
<i>"To give up your tail means</i>
<i>you can never return...</i>

00:36:31.510 --> 00:36:33.780
<i>to the Dragon Palace,"</i>
<i>he replied.</i>

00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:38.280
<i>"I don't care," she said. "So long</i>
<i>as Jiro realizes my feelings."</i>

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:42.320
<i>Saying that,</i>
<i>Nagi gave up her tail.</i>

00:37:05.150 --> 00:37:07.080
Well done, Doctor.

00:37:07.110 --> 00:37:09.140
I appreciate what you did.

00:37:19.830 --> 00:37:22.160
Here we go. And this, too. Here.

00:37:23.330 --> 00:37:25.320
The real problem
is her post-op recovery.

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:27.260
Those stomach aches, you mean?

00:37:27.400 --> 00:37:27.960
Yeah.

00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:31.200
If anything happens,
contact me any time.

00:37:31.310 --> 00:37:33.140
I'll do whatever I can.

00:37:33.880 --> 00:37:35.240
<i>The surgery was complete.</i>

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:39.310
<i>The nerves which were damaged</i>
<i>by the pressure of the deformed...</i>

00:37:39.350 --> 00:37:41.010
<i>bones and cartilage</i>
<i>have begun to recover.</i>

00:37:41.050 --> 00:37:43.740
<i>She should have</i>
<i>no more pain in her legs.</i>

00:37:44.490 --> 00:37:47.680
<i>What concerns me are the large</i>
<i>number of complications arising...</i>

00:37:47.720 --> 00:37:50.380
<i>between the duodenal</i>
<i>second position and the jejunum.</i>

00:37:51.960 --> 00:37:54.690
<i>In Tsukiko's case,</i>
<i>a detailed post-op examination...</i>

00:37:54.730 --> 00:37:56.220
<i>hasn't indicated anything yet.</i>

00:37:57.270 --> 00:37:59.960
<i>If all goes well, the stitches</i>
<i>should come out in a week.</i>

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:03.400
<i>Then we can begin rehab</i>
<i>to get her back to a normal life.</i>

00:38:03.970 --> 00:38:04.960
Here we go!

00:38:05.870 --> 00:38:09.540
Tsukiko, tell me at once
if your stomach starts hurting.

00:38:09.940 --> 00:38:11.240
My stomach doesn't hurt at all.

00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:16.910
Come back here!

00:38:17.990 --> 00:38:20.250
We'll wait and see...

00:38:20.290 --> 00:38:22.720
I planned for another
close examination.

00:38:27.190 --> 00:38:31.030
Mikazuki City Hall, huh?
Leave it to me!

00:38:31.070 --> 00:38:34.500
I heard the Mikazuki Syndrome
Relief Committee has an office there.

00:38:46.550 --> 00:38:49.380
Excuse me, I'm looking
for the office of Mr. Oida.

00:38:51.220 --> 00:38:53.690
Sorry for the wait.
You must be Mr. Hazama.

00:38:54.290 --> 00:38:56.850
Mr. Sugita from D.L. Chemical
was asking about you.

00:38:57.330 --> 00:39:00.990
There's someone who hasn't
filed a claim card,

00:39:01.030 --> 00:39:04.900
who is clearly a victim
of Mikazuki Syndrome.

00:39:05.600 --> 00:39:08.930
That's what you called about.
The girl, Tsukiko, right?

00:39:09.970 --> 00:39:12.870
Without a claim card, she'll have
to pay the doctor's bills herself.

00:39:12.910 --> 00:39:14.530
She'll be saddled
with an unpayable debt.

00:39:14.810 --> 00:39:15.470
Yes.

00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:20.280
I'd like you to issue her
a claim card at once.

00:39:22.850 --> 00:39:25.480
All right, and the reason
you can't issue one is...

00:39:26.490 --> 00:39:30.720
The truth is, I tried to issue
a card for her a long time ago!

00:39:31.490 --> 00:39:34.720
Everyone around here
knows about Tsukiko.

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:39.430
<i>She started living</i>
<i>on the beach one day.</i>

00:39:39.470 --> 00:39:41.130
<i>She's so good</i>
<i>at catching fish...</i>

00:39:41.170 --> 00:39:43.500
<i>some said she must have been</i>
<i>a mermaid in a past life.</i>

00:39:44.770 --> 00:39:48.070
<i>Her legs seemed</i>
<i>to be crippled,</i>

00:39:48.110 --> 00:39:49.970
<i>so when I heard</i>
<i>the rumors about her...</i>

00:39:51.580 --> 00:39:52.480
Miss Tsukiko!

00:39:55.750 --> 00:39:59.240
Hi, I'm from City Hall.

00:39:59.690 --> 00:40:01.150
Would you come with me
to the hospital?

00:40:01.820 --> 00:40:03.790
I'd like you to get
an examination.

00:40:03.960 --> 00:40:08.190
I can't sell my fish
in a hospital. Excuse me.

00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:11.200
Still, I didn't give up.

00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:16.470
Miss Tsukiko. Good evening.

00:40:16.640 --> 00:40:17.600
Good evening.

00:40:18.010 --> 00:40:20.630
This man says
he'd like to buy your fish.

00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:23.300
Thanks for your business.

00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:27.780
In return, will you let me
examine your legs?

00:40:28.950 --> 00:40:30.850
You can look if you like.

00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:36.150
Well, Doctor?

00:40:36.820 --> 00:40:38.020
I'm suspicious
about the density.

00:40:38.360 --> 00:40:39.920
Will you issue a certificate?

00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:40.690
I will.

00:40:42.300 --> 00:40:45.390
Could you tell me
your real name, Tsukiko?

00:40:45.430 --> 00:40:46.260
It's Tsukiko.

00:40:47.200 --> 00:40:49.900
That's your first name.
What's your family name?

00:40:50.910 --> 00:40:51.870
Tsukiko!

00:40:52.410 --> 00:40:54.530
Will you tell me
your birth date?

00:40:54.940 --> 00:40:57.240
July 7th. Tanabata.

00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:58.640
Oh, July 7th.

00:40:58.680 --> 00:41:00.740
March 3rd is Girls' Day.

00:41:01.280 --> 00:41:03.410
January 1st is New Year's!

00:41:03.750 --> 00:41:06.720
May I speak
to your mom and dad?

00:41:07.890 --> 00:41:09.220
Mom and dad?

00:41:10.490 --> 00:41:13.120
Anything about them.
Anything at all.

00:41:13.160 --> 00:41:15.720
What you remember,
what they looked like...

00:41:15.760 --> 00:41:16.700
their voices...

00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:24.570
What the hell is this?

00:41:25.040 --> 00:41:30.170
Yes, sir. It's an application for a
claim card for a girl named Tsukiko.

00:41:30.540 --> 00:41:31.530
No permanent residence.

00:41:31.580 --> 00:41:32.670
No ID number.

00:41:32.710 --> 00:41:33.810
No birth certificate.

00:41:33.850 --> 00:41:35.340
No surname. Nothing!

00:41:35.720 --> 00:41:39.050
Who'd issue a claim card
based on this?

00:41:39.950 --> 00:41:41.650
What's wrong
with her application?

00:41:41.690 --> 00:41:44.520
Handicapped people are supposed
to get preferential treatment!

00:41:46.530 --> 00:41:47.320
Redo it!

00:41:48.500 --> 00:41:52.460
If I could confirm her identity,
I could issue the card, but...

00:41:53.470 --> 00:41:55.230
That card is
an absolute necessity.

00:41:57.300 --> 00:42:00.270
I can cure her body myself...

00:42:00.570 --> 00:42:04.070
But afterwards... For her
to be able to live on her own,

00:42:04.110 --> 00:42:04.670
she needs it!

00:42:07.110 --> 00:42:07.740
Thank you.

00:42:09.820 --> 00:42:11.940
For giving Tsukiko
an ally in here.

00:42:19.460 --> 00:42:21.830
I see. We gotta
confirm her identity, huh?

00:42:21.860 --> 00:42:23.090
Figure out her background.

00:42:23.330 --> 00:42:25.490
So, she comes
from the Dragon's Palace.

00:42:25.530 --> 00:42:26.970
That'll be good enough.

00:42:27.370 --> 00:42:29.360
You idiot! How many times
do I gotta tell you?

00:42:29.400 --> 00:42:30.930
No government office
will accept that!

00:42:30.970 --> 00:42:32.500
They won't take it!

00:42:32.940 --> 00:42:33.500
Manager!

00:42:35.010 --> 00:42:39.740
Can you get me a list
of schools in the Mikazuki area?

00:42:39.780 --> 00:42:43.050
Yes... And include any schools
for the handicapped.

00:42:43.350 --> 00:42:46.440
Gotcha! I'll check
the phone book now!

00:42:46.490 --> 00:42:48.220
Wait, wait, wait!

00:42:49.420 --> 00:42:51.890
What can I do to help?

00:42:51.930 --> 00:42:55.050
Ask people around town
while you work.

00:42:55.100 --> 00:42:55.890
Roger!

00:42:55.930 --> 00:43:00.300
Concentrate on asking about
when Tsukiko first appeared in town.

00:43:00.330 --> 00:43:02.670
I'll do that on duty and off!

00:43:03.340 --> 00:43:07.030
I'll check hospital records,
especially psychiatric hospitals.

00:43:07.270 --> 00:43:10.400
And the police for any runaways
or missing persons.

00:43:11.550 --> 00:43:12.200
So?

00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:16.070
So, what should I do?

00:43:16.920 --> 00:43:18.440
Pinoko, you will assist me.

00:43:18.690 --> 00:43:20.240
Her rehab's going to begin soon.

00:43:20.290 --> 00:43:21.020
We're going to be busy!

00:43:26.090 --> 00:43:28.320
Oh, Tsuki, dear. You're awake?

00:43:29.630 --> 00:43:30.790
Me, too!

00:43:31.300 --> 00:43:33.060
I want to get in the bath, too!

00:43:36.570 --> 00:43:38.400
Don't! Your bandages
will come loose!

00:43:48.820 --> 00:43:51.480
<i>We never learned her identity.</i>

00:43:52.650 --> 00:43:54.050
Come on, stand up!

00:43:54.090 --> 00:43:54.850
Stand up!

00:43:55.960 --> 00:43:57.620
Stand up and come here!

00:43:58.260 --> 00:44:01.230
Doctor, wait. Wait there...

00:44:01.630 --> 00:44:04.100
I'm waiting!
I'm waiting right here!

00:44:10.770 --> 00:44:12.760
Don't cry! A little more!

00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:13.830
You'll be able to walk soon!

00:44:13.870 --> 00:44:15.340
Go, go, Tsukiko!

00:44:15.380 --> 00:44:16.740
Go, go, Tsukiko!

00:44:16.780 --> 00:44:18.300
Go, go, Tsukiko!

00:44:18.610 --> 00:44:21.100
Now stand!
Stand on your own feet!

00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:23.710
Now walk!
Walk on your own legs!

00:44:24.650 --> 00:44:25.240
Right!

00:44:28.890 --> 00:44:30.790
That's the way, Tsukiko!

00:44:35.530 --> 00:44:38.330
<i>A few nights later,</i>
<i>the full moon rose in the sky...</i>

00:44:39.830 --> 00:44:41.820
<i>I played my final card.</i>

00:44:43.270 --> 00:44:46.360
Doctor! Where are you going?

00:44:46.410 --> 00:44:48.570
I have some errands in town.
Where's Tsukiko?

00:44:48.610 --> 00:44:50.200
Fast, fast asleep.

00:44:50.240 --> 00:44:51.370
I'll be back before morning.

00:44:51.410 --> 00:44:52.610
Kay!

00:44:57.550 --> 00:44:59.820
D.L. Chemical, right?

00:45:02.260 --> 00:45:04.950
Doc, you know,
what we saw before...

00:45:04.990 --> 00:45:07.980
Tsuki's boobs, I mean.
Pretty, huh?

00:45:08.030 --> 00:45:11.050
So white. They looked
like an angel's!

00:45:11.100 --> 00:45:12.730
Could you not talk
for a while?

00:45:12.770 --> 00:45:14.390
Um, sorry about that.

00:45:24.880 --> 00:45:28.340
Doctor, my stomach
doesn't hurt...

00:45:29.420 --> 00:45:30.610
It doesn't hurt.

00:45:37.290 --> 00:45:38.420
Here's the south gate.

00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:40.620
Thanks. Can you
wait here for me?

00:45:40.660 --> 00:45:40.920
Sure.

00:45:46.500 --> 00:45:49.470
The executive director came
representing the president.

00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:50.630
Thanks.

00:45:50.670 --> 00:45:53.940
Well, I was thinking
of getting a new job, anyway.

00:45:59.380 --> 00:46:01.250
I'm Executive Director
Hasegawa.

00:46:01.280 --> 00:46:03.480
Sugita told me everything.

00:46:04.320 --> 00:46:06.410
You'd give yourself up?

00:46:07.220 --> 00:46:08.420
Yes.

00:46:08.460 --> 00:46:10.290
I came here at
your company's invitation,

00:46:10.820 --> 00:46:13.260
as an unlicensed doctor, to operate
on Mikazuki Syndrome patients.

00:46:13.290 --> 00:46:16.460
When I surrender, I will turn over
my records to the media.

00:46:17.770 --> 00:46:20.290
And what do you want in return?

00:46:20.770 --> 00:46:22.200
30 million yen.

00:46:22.240 --> 00:46:25.670
Reparations for a girl
who didn't receive a claims card.

00:46:26.910 --> 00:46:30.710
So, the world-famous Dr. Black Jack
is that sort of man.

00:46:30.740 --> 00:46:32.270
It's vaguely dirty.

00:46:33.080 --> 00:46:36.480
Not as much as you people
who spread your pollution!

00:46:49.960 --> 00:46:54.460
<i>Still... Dirty money</i>
<i>somehow didn't suit Tsukiko.</i>

00:46:55.270 --> 00:46:59.430
<i>I never got the chance</i>
<i>to use the money for her.</i>

00:47:05.550 --> 00:47:07.950
Doctor! Doctor!

00:47:07.980 --> 00:47:09.740
What is it? What happened?

00:47:09.780 --> 00:47:13.120
I just... I just took my eyes
off her for a little while!

00:47:13.620 --> 00:47:15.280
Doctor, read this.

00:47:18.190 --> 00:47:20.420
<i>I'm bringing you a blue pearl.</i>

00:47:22.200 --> 00:47:24.860
That fool! She can't
swim yet with those legs!

00:47:31.910 --> 00:47:33.400
Tsukiko!

00:47:33.670 --> 00:47:35.640
Tsuki!

00:47:35.680 --> 00:47:37.010
Tsukiko!

00:47:37.040 --> 00:47:38.440
Tsuki!

00:47:43.680 --> 00:47:45.740
<i>Tsukiko!</i>

00:47:46.750 --> 00:47:49.280
<i>Tsukiko!</i>

00:47:56.260 --> 00:47:56.960
<i>Five days later,</i>

00:47:58.730 --> 00:48:01.170
<i>we found Tsukiko's body...</i>

00:48:01.200 --> 00:48:02.570
<i>five meters beneath the sea.</i>

00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:14.240
<i>She loved him</i>
<i>so very, very much.</i>

00:48:14.880 --> 00:48:17.210
<i>Refusing to abandon</i>
<i>her love for Jiro,</i>

00:48:18.390 --> 00:48:21.150
<i>Nagi dove back into the sea.</i>

00:48:22.660 --> 00:48:24.680
<i>If she could just</i>
<i>get a blue pearl,</i>

00:48:25.360 --> 00:48:27.550
<i>then Jiro would</i>
<i>understand her feelings.</i>

00:48:28.130 --> 00:48:32.790
<i>But Nagi had forgotten</i>
<i>that she no longer had her tail.</i>

00:48:34.100 --> 00:48:36.400
<i>Down, down she sank,</i>

00:48:36.900 --> 00:48:39.630
<i>until finally she drowned.</i>

00:48:49.520 --> 00:48:51.250
<i>Doctor?</i>

00:48:52.320 --> 00:48:53.510
<i>Doctor, look!</i>

00:48:56.020 --> 00:48:57.220
<i>See my ocean!</i>

00:48:59.560 --> 00:49:00.790
<i>See my love!</i>

00:49:09.170 --> 00:49:12.330
<i>Doctor, I love you!</i>

00:49:14.270 --> 00:49:15.400
<i>Tsukiko...</i>

00:49:25.050 --> 00:49:26.420
Doctor!

00:49:26.950 --> 00:49:27.940
Doctor!

00:49:32.190 --> 00:49:34.180
Look! Look at this!

00:49:34.660 --> 00:49:37.960
We found this
during Tsukiko's autopsy!

00:49:39.300 --> 00:49:43.670
They were lined up from
the duodenum to the jejunum!

00:49:46.870 --> 00:49:48.360
Blue pearls!

00:49:51.710 --> 00:49:52.910
Take them.

00:49:52.950 --> 00:49:54.880
She was your patient.

00:49:56.720 --> 00:49:59.710
No. If you can,
please return them to the sea.

00:50:01.220 --> 00:50:02.280
I understand.

00:50:11.500 --> 00:50:12.660
I'll take them!

00:50:12.830 --> 00:50:15.860
They may be the key to
understanding Mikazuki Syndrome.

00:50:16.770 --> 00:50:18.100
Doctor...

00:50:26.510 --> 00:50:27.280
<i>That's right.</i>

00:50:28.580 --> 00:50:29.310
<i>That's right!</i>

00:50:30.720 --> 00:50:32.410
<i>I can't be beaten yet.</i>

00:50:33.620 --> 00:50:34.590
<i>I can't.</i>

00:51:02.220 --> 00:51:07.680
Remember when
you came to me then,

00:51:08.790 --> 00:51:14.660
trying to show me
the way that love should be?

00:51:15.430 --> 00:51:21.930
You walk alone,
step into the street,

00:51:21.970 --> 00:51:27.240
keeping an eye
looking at me.

00:51:30.180 --> 00:51:32.940
Ah, it's so dazzling bright.

00:51:36.750 --> 00:51:41.380
I have to shut my eyes.

00:51:43.360 --> 00:51:48.760
Ah, in the future facing me,

00:51:48.800 --> 00:51:55.600
the sun burns a fire so bright.
I just begin to feel its light.

00:51:56.270 --> 00:51:59.760
Just persevere,
don't shed a tear,

00:51:59.810 --> 00:52:02.470
don't give up
and fear the worst.

00:52:02.910 --> 00:52:08.810
Just trust yourself above all else.
Put your intuition first.

00:52:09.480 --> 00:52:12.880
You passed along
love so strong...

00:52:12.920 --> 00:52:16.180
it was bursting powerfully.

00:52:16.220 --> 00:52:18.890
Draw it close
to comfort me.

00:52:19.290 --> 00:52:22.730
Just persevere,
don't shed a tear,

00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:25.820
don't give up
and fear the worst.

00:52:25.870 --> 00:52:31.930
Just trust yourself above all else.
Put your intuition first.

00:52:32.440 --> 00:52:39.070
You passed along
love so strong...

00:52:39.110 --> 00:52:42.340
it was bursting powerfully.
